Decision rule applied: scalar invariance is rejected if CFI drops by more
than 0.010 or RMSEA rises by more than 0.015 relative to the metric model
(Cheung and Rensvold 2002; Chen 2007). The scaled chi-square difference
test is not used as the rule: at n = 5,068 it is significant for every
model here, including the random-split negative control, so it carries no
information about practical non-invariance.

